title: Updating the configuration
tags: Configuration
kind: guide
summary: metafolder-sync-config installs the shipped defaults, then merges each new version into your edits; a conflict changes nothing.

After pulling a new version of metafolder, apply its defaults:

```
scripts/complete-build.sh                 # builds everything, then syncs
target/debug/metafolder-sync-config       # the sync alone, from the checkout root
```

`metafolder-sync-config` is the only program that touches the configuration's git
history; it is an install step, never run by a long-lived process. `--source <dir>`
is the checkout to read the defaults from (default: the current directory),
`--config-dir <dir>` the configuration to update (default: `~/.config/metafolder/`).
It refuses a checkout whose documentation has not been rendered
(`scripts/doc build`, which `complete-build.sh` runs first — [[Building]]).

!! What it does

The first time, it creates the repository: every shipped default committed on
`default`, and `main` created at the same commit and checked out.

Afterwards:

# It builds the shipped tree and commits it on `default`, if it changed.
# If `main` already contains `default`, there is nothing to do: your working tree is left alone, uncommitted edits included.
# Otherwise it commits your uncommitted edits on `main` first, as a "user edits" commit — one conflict point, and an exact restore.
# It merges `default` into `main`: a fast-forward when you have no edits, a merge commit otherwise, then checks the result out.
# On a conflict, it resets `main` to where it stood before the merge (your edits kept, in their commit), reports the conflicting files, and changes nothing else.

A conflict left that way is reported again on the next run: "nothing to do" means
`main` contains `default`, not "the defaults did not change". Since it is a plain
git repository, you can also resolve it yourself: `git merge default` in
`~/.config/metafolder/`.

!! Going back to a default

Reverting a file to its shipped version is a git operation:

```
cd ~/.config/metafolder && git checkout default -- gui/style.css
```

The same holds for a single keybinding: `gui/keybindings.toml` is the whole set,
yours and the shipped ones merged ([[The keybindings file]]).
